Feature: Child lock
  LOCK turns the child lock on and off. While it is on, the dial and the other
  buttons do nothing, so turning the dial doesn't start the kettle.

  Expectation: Lock turns the child lock on
    Given the child lock is off
    When the user presses lock
    Then the child lock is on

  Expectation: Lock again turns it off
    Given the child lock is on
    When the user presses lock
    Then the child lock is off

  Expectation: The child lock holds the kettle while the dial turns
    Overrides: Turning the dial up starts the kettle
    Given the kettle is off
    And the child lock is on
    When the dial is above 55 %
    Then the kettle is off

  Expectation: The child lock ignores the start button
    Overrides: The start button starts the kettle
    Given the kettle is off
    And the child lock is on
    When the user presses start
    Then the kettle is off
